{:doc ["New-DSL conversion of ac/combat/abilities/rad_intensify.edn (S6). ONLY"
        ":program changes -- from the old {:component :flow/phases ...} tree to a"
        "string of new surface-DSL text, parsed via cn.li.node.surface/parse and"
        "compiled via cn.li.combat.run/compile-doc! (see ac/src/test/clojure/cn/"
        "li/ac/skills/skills_test.clj for the real compile+dispatch proof)."
        ""
        "Everything else here is verbatim from the old file, UNCHANGED: this"
        "ability's :mark-policies and :damage-policies are not node-core DSL at"
        "all -- they are consumed by cn.li.combat.damage (a verbatim port of the"
        "old aggregation algorithm's :ref/:expr tree interpreter, per this"
        "session's explicit scoping decision to only rebuild the dispatch layer,"
        "not re-derive the aggregation math through the new VM) and by the"
        "not-yet-rewritten mark-application path. Converting THOSE to the new DSL"
        "is out of scope for this pass; only the ability's own :do/:phases body"
        "(what runs when the ability activates) moves to the new pipeline."
        ""
        "rad-intensify is passive: all four phases are a bare finish, and it has"
        "no :do logic of its own -- its entire real behavior lives in"
        ":damage-policies (multiply damage while the :radiation mark is active)."
        "Picked as the FIRST S6 conversion specifically because it is close to a"
        "no-op on the :program side, letting the file-shape/loader-adjacent"
        "questions (does :program become string DSL text or nested data? does"
        ":mark-policies/:damage-policies move too?) get settled on the simplest"
        "possible case before tackling a real :do body."]
 :schema-version 2
 :kind :ability
 :id :rad-intensify
 :name-key "ability.skill.meltdowner.rad_intensify"
 :description-key "ability.skill.meltdowner.rad_intensify.desc"
 :revision 2
 :activation :passive
 :requires [:world/id]
 :prerequisites [{:skill-id :electron-bomb :min-exp 0.5}]
 :mark-policies
 [{:mark-type :radiation
   :requires-ability :rad-intensify
   :duration-ticks {:ref [:input :tunables :mark-duration-ticks]}
   :vfx {:effect-id :target-mark-session
         :operation :spawn
         :audience {:type :nearby :radius 32.0}
         :offset {:vec3 [0.0 0.8 0.0]}
         :payload {:position {:ref [:mark :target-position]}
                   :ttl-ticks {:ref [:input :tunables :mark-duration-ticks]}
                   :seed {:ref [:input :context :activation-seed]}
                   :count 3 :radius 0.35 :color [236 170 93 180]}}}]
 :tunables {:damage-rate {:curve :pair}
            :mark-duration-ticks {:curve :const :type :int}
            :mastery-denominator {:curve :const}}
 :program
 "{:ability :rad-intensify
   :activation :passive
   :tunables {:damage-rate {:type :double} :mark-duration-ticks {:type :long}
              :mastery-denominator {:type :double}}
   :phases {:start [(finish {:outcome :passive})]
            :pulse [(finish {:outcome :passive})]
            :release [(finish {:outcome :passive})]
            :abort [(finish {:outcome :passive})]}}"
 :damage-policies
 [{:on :combat/damage
   :priority 100
   :mark-type :radiation
   :when {:expr :bool/and
          :args [{:ref [:input :context :mark?]}
                 {:expr :math/gt :args [{:ref [:input :request :base]} 0.0]}]}
   :program {:component :damage/multiply :multiplier {:ref [:input :context :mark :rate]}}}]
 :costs nil
 :cooldown nil
 :progression nil
 :invariants nil}
